              <td>160-200</td>
              <td>Casual professional, comfortable</td>
              <td>Hospitality, retail, casual</td>
              <td>$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Trousers & Pants</td>
              <td>200-250</td>
              <td>Durable, professional fit, consistent</td>
              <td>Formal, business casual, industrial</td>
              <td>$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Aprons & Workwear</td>
              <td>180-220</td>
              <td>Stain resistant, functional, durable</td>
              <td>Service industries, hospitality</td>
              <td>$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Jackets & Blazers</td>
              <td>200-280</td>
              <td>Formal, layered, professional</td>
              <td>Formal roles, seasonal</td>
              <td>$$$</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
          <caption>All categories available from 300 pieces minimum. Custom programs available.</caption>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Production Process</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Our Manufacturing Process</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Our corporate uniform manufacturing follows a structured process designed to ensure consistent quality, fit accuracy, and professional appearance. The process typically spans 60-75 days for first-time orders including sampling and production, with 45-60 days for repeat orders using approved fabrics and patterns. Corporate uniforms require particular attention to fit consistency and durability for industrial laundering.</p>
        
        <p>The process begins with specification review, where we analyze your requirements including fabric preferences, garment type, size chart, branding requirements, and industry-specific needs. Our team provides feedback on technical feasibility and may suggest modifications to optimize manufacturability while maintaining design intent. This stage takes 2-3 days and ensures technical alignment before sampling begins. For corporate uniforms, we pay particular attention to sizing consistency and durability requirements.</p>
        
        <p>Fabric sourcing and development follows specification review, taking 10-15 days for standard fabrics and 15-20 days for custom fabric development. Corporate uniform fabrics undergo testing for durability, color fastness, and shrinkage resistance before approval. We test fabrics for industrial laundering durability when applicable. All fabrics must meet OEKO-TEX Standard 100 requirements and any industry-specific certifications such as flame resistance. If you require custom fabric development for specific colors or performance properties, we coordinate with mills to produce sample yardage.</p>
        
        <p>Sample development for corporate uniforms takes 15-20 days for basic items and 20-25 days for complex garments with specialized features. Initial samples focus on construction and basic fit, with subsequent samples refining fit details, fabric quality, and finish quality. We provide detailed measurement reports comparing samples to your specifications and conduct wash testing to verify dimensional stability. Corporate uniform samples require particular attention to fit consistency and durability. You may request multiple sample rounds to perfect the design.</p>
        
        <p>Fit consistency testing is a critical step in corporate uniform sampling that we conduct on all samples. We verify that measurements are consistent across the size range, ensuring uniform appearance within teams. For shirts and blouses, we check that collar sizing and sleeve lengths scale proportionally. For trousers, we verify that waist and inseam measurements maintain consistent relationships across sizes. This consistency testing ensures that employees wearing different sizes present a cohesive uniform appearance, which is essential for professional branding.</p>
        
        <p>Pattern grading for corporate uniforms requires careful attention to proportional scaling to ensure consistent fit across sizes. The relationship between various measurements must be maintained through grading to ensure that different sizes present a consistent silhouette. Our pattern makers use graded measurement systems that account for these relationships, producing size sets from XS to 3XL that maintain proportional fit. Grading takes 3-5 days for basic items and 5-7 days for complex garments with multiple components. Grading includes verification of consistency across the size range.</p>
        
        <p>Bulk production for corporate uniforms spans 30-40 days from fabric receipt for basic items such as polo shirts and simple trousers. Shirts and blouses typically require 35-45 days. Cutting is performed with attention to grain direction for woven items to ensure consistent appearance. Sewing lines are staffed by operators trained in professional garment construction, with particular expertise in durable seam techniques, secure button attachment, and professional finishing. Quality checkpoints at each sewing operation verify seam integrity, construction accuracy, and professional finish.</p>
        
        <p>Final quality inspection uses AQL 2.5 standards for major defects and AQL 4.0 for minor defects, with additional testing for corporate uniform-specific criteria. Inspection includes measurement verification against graded size charts, wash testing on random samples to verify dimensional stability, and construction quality verification. We also conduct durability testing on critical seams and closures. Detailed inspection reports with photos are provided before shipment, and any defects found are rectified before goods leave our facility.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Materials</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Fabric & Material Options</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Fabric selection is critical to corporate uniform performance, affecting durability, comfort, professional appearance, and care requirements. We offer multiple fabric options optimized for different industries and work environments. All fabrics are tested for durability and professional appearance.</p>
        
        <p>Cotton/polyester blends are the traditional choice for corporate uniforms, providing natural comfort from cotton with the durability and wrinkle resistance of polyester. Typical blends range from 65/35 to 50/50 cotton-polyester ratios, with higher cotton content providing more natural feel. These blends typically range from 180-220 GSM and offer balanced performance at competitive prices. The polyester component reduces shrinkage and wrinkling compared to 100% cotton, improving dimensional stability and appearance maintenance. Cotton/polyester blends are ideal for general corporate uniforms where professional appearance and durability are priorities.</p>
        
        <p>Performance fabrics incorporate moisture-wicking technology to keep wearers comfortable in active roles. These fabrics typically range from 160-200 GSM and may include additional features like antimicrobial treatments, UV protection, or stretch for mobility. Performance fabrics are particularly suitable for uniforms in hospitality, healthcare, and active professional roles where employees are physically active throughout their shifts. These fabrics cost approximately 15-20% more than standard blends but provide enhanced comfort and functionality.</p>
        
        <p>Flame-resistant fabrics meet safety standards for industrial environments where fire hazards exist. These fabrics are typically treated cotton or cotton/polyester blends in weights ranging from 200-250 GSM. Flame resistance can be achieved through chemical treatments or inherently flame-resistant fibers like modacrylic. These fabrics meet specific safety standards such as NFPA 2112 for flash fire resistance. Flame-resistant uniforms are essential for industrial, manufacturing, and utility environments where worker safety is paramount. Flame-resistant fabrics cost approximately 25-30% more than standard fabrics.</p>
        
        <p>Stain-resistant fabrics incorporate treatments that repel liquids and resist staining, making them ideal for hospitality and food service industries. These fabrics typically use cotton/polyester blends with stain-resistant treatments applied during finishing. The treatments help uniforms maintain clean appearance through spills and frequent laundering. Stain-resistant fabrics are particularly valuable in restaurants, cafes, and healthcare settings where stains are common. These fabrics cost approximately 10-15% more than untreated blends but reduce replacement frequency and maintain professional appearance longer.</p>
        
        <p>Organic cotton certified by GOTS provides sustainable options for companies prioritizing environmental responsibility. Organic cotton is grown without synthetic pesticides or fertilizers and processed without harmful chemicals. The fabric maintains the same comfort and performance as conventional cotton with the added benefit of environmental certification. Organic cotton typically costs 15-20% more than conventional cotton but enables sustainability claims that appeal to environmentally conscious companies and consumers. GOTS certification provides verification of organic content throughout the supply chain.</p>
        
        <p>All corporate uniform fabrics undergo OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification testing for harmful substances including heavy metals, pesticides, formaldehyde, and other chemicals. This certification is essential for professional workwear due to prolonged skin contact during work shifts. We provide OEKO-TEX certificates for each fabric lot, enabling you to substantiate safety claims in your internal documentation and meet regulatory requirements for workplace safety.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Fabric</th>
              <th>GSM Range</th>
              <th>Key Properties</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
              <th>Price Tier</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Cotton/Polyester Blends</td>
              <td>180-220</td>
              <td>Durable, wrinkle resistant, professional</td>
              <td>General corporate, professional</td>
              <td>$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Performance Fabrics</td>
              <td>160-200</td>
              <td>Moisture-wicking, comfortable, active</td>
              <td>Hospitality, healthcare, active</td>
              <td>$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Flame-Resistant Fabrics</td>
              <td>200-250</td>
              <td>Safety compliant, industrial, protective</td>
              <td>Industrial, manufacturing, utility</td>
              <td>$$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Stain-Resistant Fabrics</td>
              <td>180-220</td>
              <td>Stain repellent, clean appearance, durable</td>
              <td>Food service, hospitality, healthcare</td>
              <td>$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Organic Cotton</td>
              <td>180-220</td>
              <td>Sustainable, natural, certified</td>
              <td>Eco-conscious companies</td>
              <td>$$$</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
          <caption>All fabrics OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certified. Custom treatments available.</caption>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Bangladesh Advantage</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Why Source Corporate Uniforms from Bangladesh</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Bangladesh has established itself as a competitive sourcing destination for corporate uniforms and workwear, combining cost advantages with developing expertise in professional garment production. The country's garment industry includes numerous factories focused on shirts, trousers, and workwear, with established supply chains for professional fabrics. This specialization, combined with competitive labor costs, makes Bangladesh an attractive option for corporate uniform manufacturing.</p>
        
        <p>Labor costs in Bangladesh are significantly lower than in China, Vietnam, or Turkey, translating to 15-25% cost savings on finished corporate uniforms. However, the cost advantage does not come at the expense of quality. The Bangladeshi garment industry has developed particular expertise in professional garment production, with operators skilled in shirt construction, trouser tailoring, and workwear manufacturing. Our facility conducts regular training programs to ensure operators are proficient in the latest professional garment construction techniques.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh's textile infrastructure includes weaving mills capable of producing cotton/polyester blends and other professional fabrics suitable for uniforms. The country has invested in weaving capacity for shirting and trouser fabrics, reducing reliance on imported materials for basic uniform styles. This local sourcing reduces lead times and logistics costs compared to countries that rely entirely on imported fabrics. Our relationships with local weaving mills ensure priority allocation and consistent quality for uniform fabrics. For specialized fabrics, we maintain relationships with international fabric suppliers.</p>
        
        <p>The country's export infrastructure includes experienced freight forwarders, customs brokers, and documentation specialists familiar with garment export requirements. Shipments from Bangladesh to major markets are routine, with multiple weekly sailings to Europe and North America. Ocean freight is particularly cost-effective for corporate uniforms given the efficient container utilization. The established export infrastructure reduces the risk of delays and documentation errors that can occur with less experienced sourcing locations.</p>
        
        <p>Social compliance and workplace safety have improved significantly in Bangladesh's garment industry following comprehensive reforms after 2013. Our facility holds BSCI certification, demonstrating adherence to international labor standards including fair wages, reasonable working hours, and safe working conditions. These certifications are increasingly important to corporations that prioritize ethical sourcing in their supply chains. The improved compliance environment reduces reputational risk for brands sourcing from Bangladesh.</p>
        
        <p>Duty-free access to European markets through the Everything But Arms (EBA) arrangement provides Bangladesh garments with preferential tariff treatment, reducing import costs for EU customers. Similar preferential access exists for other markets including Canada, Australia, and Japan. This duty advantage can significantly impact landed costs for corporate uniforms, which are subject to standard garment duty rates in many markets. For businesses targeting EU distribution, the duty savings can substantially improve overall margins.</p>
        
        <p>The Bangladesh garment industry has developed specialized expertise in professional garment production, which directly translates to corporate uniform manufacturing. Producing consistent shirt collars, tailored trousers, and professional finishes that maintain appearance through repeated laundering are well-established skills in the country's workforce. This specialized expertise reduces the learning curve for new uniform styles and ensures consistent quality across production runs. The industry's experience with international corporate wear brands also means that professional quality standards are well-understood.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">International Shipping</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Shipping to UK, USA, Australia & EU</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>We ship corporate uniforms to major international markets including the United Kingdom, United States, Australia, and European Union countries. Each market has specific requirements for documentation, duties, and shipping timelines that we navigate routinely. Our experience with international uniform shipments ensures your goods arrive on time and with proper documentation for customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>Shipments to the United Kingdom typically take 30-35 days by ocean freight, including transit time and customs clearance. Air freight options reduce this to 7-10 days at significantly higher cost. The UK applies import duties on garments from Bangladesh, though rates vary by garment type and fabric composition. Corporate uniforms typically fall under specific HS codes for shirts, trousers, or workwear. We provide accurate classification and valuation to ensure proper duty calculation. Post-Brexit documentation requirements are handled to ensure smooth customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>United States shipments take 25-30 days by ocean freight to West Coast ports and 35-40 days to East Coast ports. Air freight takes 5-7 days to major US airports. The US maintains normal trade relations with Bangladesh, with standard MFN duty rates applying to corporate uniforms. The US has specific labeling requirements for garments including fiber content in English and country of origin. We ensure all labels meet US Federal Trade Commission requirements. US customs compliance is handled through proper documentation and accurate classification.</p>
        
        <p>Australia shipments take 20-25 days by ocean freight to major ports including Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane. Air freight takes 7-10 days. Australia maintains a free trade agreement with Bangladesh that eliminates duties on many garments when rules of origin are met. We ensure our production processes meet these origin requirements to qualify for duty-free entry. Australia's strict biosecurity requirements are addressed through proper packaging and documentation to prevent clearance delays.</p>
        
        <p>European Union shipments benefit from duty-free access under the Everything But Arms arrangement. Ocean freight takes 28-32 days to Northern European ports and 32-38 days to Southern European ports. Air freight takes 5-8 days. EU countries require specific documentation including certificates of origin, commercial invoices with detailed descriptions, and conformity declarations for certain materials. The EU also has specific requirements for textile labeling including fiber content percentages and care instructions in the language of the destination country.</p>
        
        <p>Documentation for all markets includes commercial invoices, packing lists, bills of lading, certificates of origin, and any required certificates for regulated materials. For corporate uniforms, this may include certificates for flame resistance when applicable. We provide all documentation in English and can arrange for translations if required by specific markets. Our documentation is prepared to meet both customs requirements and your internal accounting needs, with clear descriptions and accurate valuations.</p>
        
        <p>Incoterms can be structured according to your preferences, including FOB (Free On Board) Bangladesh for maximum control, CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) to destination port for convenience, or DDP (Delivered Duty Paid) for complete door-to-door service. For corporate uniforms, we typically recommend FOB for experienced importers with established freight forwarding relationships, as this typically provides the best overall cost. CIF and DDP options are available for businesses seeking simplified logistics.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Certifications</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Quality Standards & Certifications</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Quality assurance and certification are fundamental to our corporate uniform manufacturing process. Corporate uniforms require particular attention to consistency and durability for professional appearance and industrial laundering. We maintain multiple certifications that verify our commitment to quality, social responsibility, and environmental standards.</p>
        
        <p>ISO 9001 certification applies to our quality management system, ensuring consistent processes for production and quality control. ISO 9001 requires documented procedures for all critical processes, regular internal audits, and continuous improvement. This certification provides assurance that our quality systems are systematic and repeatable, reducing variability between production runs. For corporate uniforms, this means consistent fit, fabric quality, and construction across orders.</p>
        
        <p>BSCI (Business Social Compliance Initiative) certification verifies our adherence to international labor standards including fair wages, reasonable working hours, prohibition of child labor, and safe working conditions. BSCI audits are conducted by independent third-party auditors and cover all aspects of social compliance. This certification is important for corporations that prioritize ethical sourcing and need to demonstrate supply chain responsibility to stakeholders and increasingly conscious consumers.</p>
        
        <p>OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification applies to all our corporate uniform fabrics, ensuring they are free from harmful substances including heavy metals, pesticides, formaldehyde, and other chemicals. This certification is particularly important for workwear with prolonged skin contact during work shifts. OEKO-TEX testing covers all fabric components including base materials, threads, trims, and buttons. We provide OEKO-TEX certificates for each material lot, enabling you to substantiate safety claims in your internal documentation.</p>
        
        <p>Flame resistance certification applies to our flame-resistant fabrics, ensuring they meet specific safety standards such as NFPA 2112 for flash fire resistance. These certifications are essential for industrial uniforms used in hazardous environments where fire safety is critical. We maintain certification documentation for all flame-resistant garments, enabling compliance with workplace safety regulations and providing assurance to workers and regulatory bodies.</p>
        
        <p>WRAP (Worldwide Responsible Accredited Production) certification is another social compliance certification we maintain, focusing specifically on workplace conditions and worker rights. WRAP certification covers similar ground to BSCI but with different audit methodology and emphasis. Holding multiple social compliance certifications provides flexibility to meet various corporate requirements, as different companies may specify different certification preferences in their supplier codes of conduct.</p>
        
        <p>Internal quality control processes supplement these certifications with day-to-day assurance specific to corporate uniform production. We conduct in-line inspections during production, measuring garments at critical checkpoints to verify dimensional accuracy. Final inspection includes wash testing on random samples to verify dimensional stability and ensure garments maintain their fit after industrial laundering. We maintain records of all testing results, enabling traceability if issues arise after delivery.</p>
      </div>
