  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Getting Started</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">How to Get Started</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Starting your corporate uniform production with SDF Clothing follows a structured process designed to ensure your requirements are met and quality expectations are understood from the outset. The process begins with providing detailed specifications, after which we guide you through sampling, fit verification, and production.</p>
        
        <p>Step one is to submit your technical specifications through our contact form or email. Essential information for corporate uniforms includes: fabric preference, garment type, size chart or employee sizing, branding requirements (logo placement, embroidery specifications), industry-specific requirements, target quantity per style and color, and desired delivery timeline. If you have technical drawings, photos of reference samples, or existing uniforms you want to replicate, include these for clarity.</p>
        
        <p>Step two involves our technical review and quotation process. Within 24-48 hours of receiving your specifications, we provide a detailed quotation including fabric costs, production costs, branding costs, and estimated shipping costs. The quotation specifies lead times for sampling and production, minimum order quantities, and payment terms. For corporate uniforms, we clarify industry-specific requirements and ensure all fabrics meet applicable safety standards. You may request revisions to the quotation to adjust specifications to meet budget targets.</p>
        
        <p>Step three is sample development and approval. After quotation acceptance, we proceed with sample development, typically taking 15-20 days for basic items and 20-25 days for complex garments. Samples are shipped to you for review, and we provide detailed measurement reports. For corporate uniforms, we recommend fit testing samples to verify consistency across sizes and overall professional appearance. You may approve samples as-is, request modifications to fit or fabric, or proceed with additional sample rounds.</p>
        
        <p>Step four is production confirmation. Once samples are approved and fit consistency is verified, we require a deposit to confirm production and initiate fabric procurement. Standard terms are 30% deposit with order confirmation and 70% before shipment. Production begins after deposit receipt and fabric availability is confirmed. We provide a production schedule with key milestones including cutting completion, sewing completion, and expected shipment date. Throughout production, we provide status updates.</p>
        
        <p>Step five is final inspection and shipment. Before shipment, we conduct final quality inspection using AQL standards with additional testing for corporate uniform-specific criteria including fit consistency verification. We provide an inspection report for your review. Once inspection is approved, we finalize packaging with your branding elements and prepare shipping documentation including all required certificates. Balance payment is required before release of shipping documents.</p>
        
        <p>Throughout the process, our team provides technical guidance on uniform construction, fabric selection, and branding optimization. We understand that corporate uniforms require consistent quality and professional appearance to maintain brand image and employee satisfaction. Clear communication about requirements and expectations helps us deliver products that meet professional standards.</p>
      </div>
